Pyxis builds upstream sources as a static library with eight patches:
the dynamic API is off, the Pyxis video and audio drivers are registered, and the Steam
virtual gamepad file is not read because Pyxis stat has no modification time,
and Pyxis pointer positions, warp and lock are authoritative in SDL mouse core.
The timer thread starts at the first timer, and SDL_Quit always stops it.
A private Pyxis event identity follows physical clipboard commands through
the original queue node; shared commands change only their event modifiers.
Native opposite scroll increments cancel fractional wheel residue, and the
public mouse-button mask uses an unsigned shift to represent button 32.
The patches retain SDL's zlib license.

The Pyxis backend in pyxis/ (video, OpenGL, input, clipboard, audio, timer, threads and paths) and SDL_config.h
are original Pyxis material under the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0;
see the ports repository's LICENSE and LICENSING.md. The backend uses the
shared US key layout exported by the Pyxis SDK.

The ordinary libSDL2.a has no OpenGL backend or Mesa/C++ dependency. The
separate libSDL2-osmesa.a compiles the Pyxis backend with PYXIS_USE_OSMESA and
binds statically to Mesa softpipe; select it instead of the ordinary archive.
Both use the same SDL API and public headers. Covered backend source and build
configuration are retained in sdl2-dev at share/sources/sdl2; the OSMesa
development package depends on sdl2-dev, mesa-dev and libcxx-dev. Static
consumers must retain Mesa and C++ runtime notices as well.

Audio capture, haptics, sensors, HIDAPI, shared objects, Vulkan, SDL_main and
SDL_test are not built. No host libc or compatibility
stubs are included.

The opt-in manual SDL clipboard exercise in manual/ is original Pyxis material
under MPL-2.0. Its small bitmap glyph rows follow the native mousetest tool.
